== Mypy — Type Health

#rect(fill: rgb("#fff8e8"), stroke: 1.5pt, inset: 10pt)\[\[#text(size: 9pt)\[\[
  *Exit code 1 — 62 errors in 8 files*

  *File*        *Errors*  *Pattern*
  gui_service.py    46     default=settings.<field> in number_control()
                       NiceGUI field.value is Any; float() cast fails
  supervisor.py      9     PlotterDaemon arg union:
                       firebase_remote | \_local_only → constructor expects firebase_remote only
  gui_support.py     4     Same settings.<field> propagation
  preflight.py       2     check_tinybee_hardware type mismatch
  svg_gcode.py        0    Clean — 30+ fully-typed functions
  store.py            0    Clean
  transport.py        0    Clean

  *Recommended:* wrap each default=settings.<field> with float(settings.<field> or 0.0);
  OR annotate GuiSettings fields as explicit float. The root cause is
  NiceGUI dynamic field access: fields\[\["x"].value is inferred as Any | object.
